#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/029_herbs_for_the_lakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Herbs for the Lakes"
msgstr "Urter til søerne"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/029_herbs_for_the_lakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Autumn comes, and the animals catch colds. Take my herbs to those who need them: two bundles to "
"the horse farm, two to the herders, two to Gudrun's inn."
msgstr ""
"Efteråret kommer, og dyrene bliver forkølede. Bring mine urter til dem, der har brug for dem: to "
"bundter til hestegården, to til hyrderne, to til Gudruns kro."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/029_herbs_for_the_lakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Herbs from Tova! Now the cow and the calf stay well all winter."
msgstr "Urter fra Tova! Nu holder koen og kalven sig raske hele vinteren."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/029_herbs_for_the_lakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "All delivered? You are real helpers now. Take these herbs for your own animals."
msgstr ""
"Alt er afleveret? {crew|Du er en rigtig hjælper|Du er en rigtig hjælper|I er rigtige hjælpere} nu."
" Tag de her urter til {crew|dine|dine|jeres} egne dyr."

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/029_herbs_for_the_lakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Herbs"
msgstr "Urter"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/029_herbs_for_the_lakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "{count|a bundle of herbs|{count} bundles of herbs}"
msgstr "{count|et bundt urter|{count} bundter urter}"

#. the thing '{count|a bundle of herbs|{count} bundles of herbs}' for {thing@acc} in the
#. translations: the accusative (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty
#. if it is the same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/029_herbs_for_the_lakes/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "{count|a bundle of herbs|{count} bundles of herbs}"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/029_herbs_for_the_lakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Healers dried herbs in bundles under the roof, to have them all winter."
msgstr "Helbrederne tørrede urter i bundter under taget for at have dem hele vinteren."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/030_the_mill_turns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Mill Turns"
msgstr "Møllen drejer"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/030_the_mill_turns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The harvest is in, and the mill wheel turns day and night! But the farmers are slow. Bring me six "
"crates of grain to grind."
msgstr ""
"Høsten er i hus, og møllehjulet drejer dag og nat! Men bønderne er langsomme. Bring mig seks "
"kasser korn at male."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/030_the_mill_turns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Six crates! Listen to the stones grind. Bjarne says hello, and here is your share."
msgstr "Seks kasser! Hør stenene male. Bjarne siger hej, og her er {crew|din|din|jeres} andel."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/030_the_mill_turns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Most vikings ground their grain by hand with two stones; a water mill was a wonder."
msgstr "De fleste vikinger malede deres korn i hånden med to sten; en vandmølle var et vidunder."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/031_a_henhouse_full/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A Henhouse Full"
msgstr "Et fuldt hønsehus"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/031_a_henhouse_full/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Eggs sell so well! Let us have six hens. Buy hens at the market in Kråkhamn or the farm of "
"Frosttorp, and bring them home."
msgstr ""
"Æg sælger så godt! Lad os få seks høns. Køb høns på markedet i Kråkhamn eller på gården i "
"Frosttorp, og bring dem hjem."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/031_a_henhouse_full/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Six hens! Cluck, cluck, scratch, scratch. Do not forget: they eat grain."
msgstr "Seks høns! Kluk, kluk, skrab, skrab. Glem ikke: de spiser korn."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/031_a_henhouse_full/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Viking hens were small and laid fewer eggs than ours, but every farm had some."
msgstr "Vikingernes høns var små og lagde færre æg end vores, men alle gårde havde nogle."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Honey Cakes"
msgstr "Honningkager"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"We want to sell honey cakes on the market! But we have no oven. Bring honey and grain to your "
"grandmother; she bakes them overnight, and you bring us the cakes."
msgstr ""
"Vi vil sælge honningkager på markedet! Men vi har ingen ovn. Bring honning og korn til "
"{crew|din|din|jeres} bedstemor; hun bager dem i nat, og så bringer {crew|du|du|I} os kagerne."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Honey! Now the grain."
msgstr "Honning! Nu kornet."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "I bake them tonight. Come for them in the morning!"
msgstr "Jeg bager dem i nat. Kom og hent dem i morgen tidlig!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Still warm. Do not eat them all on the way!"
msgstr "Stadig varme. Spis dem nu ikke alle sammen på vejen!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "They smell so good! Everybody comes to our stall. Here, half the silver is yours."
msgstr ""
"De dufter så godt! Alle kommer hen til vores bod. Her, halvdelen af sølvet er "
"{crew|dit|dit|jeres}."

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cakes"
msgstr "Kager"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "{count|a basket of honey cakes|{count} baskets of honey cakes}"
msgstr "{count|en kurv honningkager|{count} kurve honningkager}"

#. the thing '{count|a basket of honey cakes|{count} baskets of honey cakes}' for {thing@acc} in the
#. translations: the accusative (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty
#. if it is the same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "{count|a basket of honey cakes|{count} baskets of honey cakes}"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Viking bread was flat and baked on hot stones; honey made it a treat."
msgstr "Vikingernes brød var fladt og bagt på varme sten; med honning blev det en godbid."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/033_the_chieftains_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Chieftain's Feast"
msgstr "Høvdingens fest"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/033_the_chieftains_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My daughter Thora turns twelve! A feast with the whole valley: bring me three crates of mead and "
"two of cheese, within three days."
msgstr ""
"Min datter Thora fylder tolv! En fest for hele dalen: bring mig tre kasser mjød og to kasser ost "
"inden for tre dage."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/033_the_chieftains_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The mead! The skalds will sing."
msgstr "Mjøden! Skjaldene skal synge."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/033_the_chieftains_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cheese, mead, songs and a fire! Come in, sit by me: it is the best birthday ever."
msgstr "Ost, mjød, sang og et bål! Kom ind, sid ved mig: det er den bedste fødselsdag nogensinde."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/033_the_chieftains_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A chieftain's hall had a long fire in the middle, and benches along the walls."
msgstr "En høvdings hal havde et langt ildsted i midten og bænke langs væggene."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Ferryman's Tale"
msgstr "Halvards fortælling"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Old Halvard told a story here last night: a hidden cove, where the swans of the lakes are born. He"
" says: ask the potter, the miller and the old man of Svanetorp."
msgstr ""
"Gamle Halvard fortalte en historie her i går aftes: om en skjult vig, hvor søernes svaner bliver "
"født. Han siger: spørg pottemageren, mølleren og den gamle mand i Svanetorp."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The cove? My grandmother said: it lies where the reeds grow tallest. Ask Astrid."
msgstr "Vigen? Min bedstemor sagde: den ligger, hvor sivene gror højest. Spørg Astrid."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Reeds? The tallest ones grow south, by Svanetorp. Go to Grim."
msgstr "Siv? De højeste gror mod syd, ved Svanetorp. Tag hen til Grim."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"So you found my secret. Behind my farm, in the reeds: the swan cove. Look, the cygnets! Grey and "
"fluffy. Tell no one!"
msgstr ""
"Så {crew|du|du|I} fandt min hemmelighed. Bag min gård, i sivene: svanevigen. Se, ungerne! Grå og "
"dunede. Sig det ikke til nogen!"

#. a gift for a task: 'You get ...'
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "the secret of the swan cove"
msgstr "hemmeligheden om svanevigen"

#. the thing 'the secret of the swan cove' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative (the
#. direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the plain
#. translation
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "the secret of the swan cove"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Young swans are grey, not white; they are called cygnets."
msgstr "Unge svaner er grå, ikke hvide; de kaldes svaneunger."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/035_wool_for_the_winter_cloth/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Wool for the Winter Cloth"
msgstr "Uld til vintertøjet"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/035_wool_for_the_winter_cloth/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Everybody wants warm cloth for the winter, and my looms are hungry. Bring me four crates of wool, "
"and I give you a bolt of red cloth."
msgstr ""
"Alle vil have varmt klæde til vinteren, og mine væve er sultne. Bring mig fire kasser uld, så "
"giver jeg {crew|dig|dig|jer} en rulle rødt klæde."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/035_wool_for_the_winter_cloth/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Clack, clack, goes the loom. Here: the reddest cloth I ever made, for you."
msgstr ""
"Klak, klak, siger væven. Her: det rødeste klæde, jeg nogensinde har lavet, til {crew|dig|dig|jer}."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/035_wool_for_the_winter_cloth/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The women of a viking farm wove all the cloth: sails, clothes and blankets."
msgstr "Kvinderne på en vikingegård vævede alt klædet: sejl, tøj og tæpper."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flax in the Field"
msgstr "Hør på marken"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Linen is softer than wool on the skin. Plant flax on your farm! When it blooms blue and is ripe, "
"bring me two crates."
msgstr ""
"Linned er blødere end uld mod huden. Så hør på {crew|din|din|jeres} gård! Når den blomstrer blåt "
"og er moden, så bring mig to kasser."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flax seed in the field. In a few days, it blooms blue."
msgstr "Hørfrø i marken. Om et par dage blomstrer den blåt."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Your own flax! I will make you linen shirts, soft as a cloud."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Din|Din|Jeres} egen hør! Jeg syr linnedskjorter til {crew|dig|dig|jer}, bløde som en sky."

#. a gift for a task: 'You get ...'
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "linen shirts"
msgstr "linnedskjorter"

#. the thing 'linen shirts' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative (the direct object),
#. e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "linen shirts"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flax was soaked, beaten and combed for weeks before it could be spun into linen."
msgstr "Hør blev udblødt, banket og kartet i ugevis, før den kunne spindes til linned."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/037_barley_for_the_brewer/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Barley for the Brewer"
msgstr "Byg til bryggeren"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/037_barley_for_the_brewer/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Orm of Hallvik wants the biggest barrel of ale for the autumn feast. I need grain, five crates! "
"Bring them, and you get two crates of my ale."
msgstr ""
"Orm fra Hallvik vil have den største tønde øl til høstfesten. Jeg skal bruge korn, fem kasser! "
"Bring dem, så får {crew|du|du|I} to kasser af mit øl."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/037_barley_for_the_brewer/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Into the water with it, let it sprout... In a week, the best ale of the lakes!"
msgstr "Ned i vandet med det, lad det spire... Om en uge: det bedste øl på søerne!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/037_barley_for_the_brewer/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ale was brewed from barley and water, often with herbs instead of hops."
msgstr "Øl blev brygget af byg og vand, tit med urter i stedet for humle."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A Proper Hold"
msgstr "Et ordentligt lastrum"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You are real traders now: you need a real hold! Bring me eight planks from Frosttorp and two "
"crates of iron tools, and pay 20 silver. Then your hold takes two more crates."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Du er en rigtig handelsmand|Du er en rigtig handelskvinde|I er rigtige handelsfolk|I er "
"rigtige handelskvinder} nu: {crew|du|du|I} skal have et rigtigt lastrum! Bring mig otte planker "
"fra Frosttorp og to kasser jernværktøj, og betal 20 sølv. Så kan {crew|dit|dit|jeres} lastrum tage"
" to kasser mere."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Planks of pine, split with wedges. Stack them well!"
msgstr "Planker af fyrretræ, kløvet med kiler. Stabl dem godt!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Good iron! Now my wages."
msgstr "Godt jern! Nu min løn."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Saw, plane, rivets... Look at her! Longer, wider, and room for two more crates."
msgstr "Sav, høvl, nitter... Se hende bare! Længere, bredere og plads til to kasser mere."

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json data/missions/055_the_great_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Plank"
msgstr "Planke"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json data/missions/055_the_great_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "{count|a plank|{count} planks}"
msgstr "{count|en planke|{count} planker}"

#. the thing '{count|a plank|{count} planks}' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative
#. (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the
#. plain translation
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json data/missions/055_the_great_hold/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "{count|a plank|{count} planks}"
