#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Viking boats were built of overlapping planks, held with iron rivets."
msgstr "Vikingebåde blev bygget af planker, der lå over hinanden, holdt sammen med jernnitter."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Messenger's Cold"
msgstr "Ingas forkølelse"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Atchoo! I have a cold, and I must tell the smith, the horse farm and the herders about the autumn "
"feast at Hallvik. Can you do it today? Atchoo!"
msgstr ""
"Atju! Jeg er forkølet, og jeg skal fortælle smeden, hestegården og hyrderne om høstfesten i "
"Hallvik. Kan {crew|du|du|I} gøre det i dag? Atju!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The autumn feast? I will bring my best knives to show."
msgstr "Høstfesten? Jeg tager mine bedste knive med og viser dem frem."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "We will come with all the horses! Tell Inga to drink hot honey water."
msgstr "Vi kommer med alle hestene! Sig til Inga, at hun skal drikke varmt honningvand."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A feast! I will bring my flute. Thank you!"
msgstr "En fest! Jeg tager min fløjte med. Tak!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Messengers rowed, rode and ran: news could cross a land in a few days."
msgstr "Budbringere roede, red og løb: nyt kunne krydse et land på få dage."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/040_hay_for_frosttorp/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hay for Frosttorp"
msgstr "Hø til Frosttorp"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/040_hay_for_frosttorp/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My hay meadow was flooded, and the cows are hungry! I need eight crates of hay. Your big boat can "
"do it in one trip."
msgstr ""
"Min høeng blev oversvømmet, og køerne er sultne! Jeg skal bruge otte kasser hø. "
"{crew|Din|Din|Jeres} store båd kan klare det på én tur."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/040_hay_for_frosttorp/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Moo! Listen to them, they are happy. You saved my winter. Take this cheese."
msgstr "Muh! Hør dem, de er glade. {crew|Du|Du|I} reddede min vinter. Tag den her ost."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/040_hay_for_frosttorp/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hay is dried grass; without enough of it, a farm could not keep its animals over winter."
msgstr "Hø er tørret græs; uden nok af det kunne en gård ikke holde sine dyr vinteren over."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Sigvor's Cheese"
msgstr "Sigvors ost"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My goats gave so much milk this summer! I made four big wheels of cheese for Orm's autumn feast in"
" Hallvik, but my boat is full of goats. Will you carry them?"
msgstr ""
"Mine geder gav så meget mælk i sommer! Jeg lavede fire store oste til Orms høstfest i Hallvik, men"
" min båd er fuld af geder. Vil {crew|du|du|I} fragte dem?"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Sigvor's cheese! The guests will fight over it. Well, not fight: they will ask nicely."
msgstr "Sigvors ost! Gæsterne kommer til at slås om den. Nå, ikke slås: de spørger pænt."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Roll them in gently. And no nibbling!"
msgstr "Rul dem forsigtigt ind. Og ingen smagsprøver!"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cheese"
msgstr "Ost"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "{count|a wheel of cheese|{count} wheels of cheese}"
msgstr "{count|en stor ost|{count} store oste}"

#. the thing '{count|a wheel of cheese|{count} wheels of cheese}' for {thing@acc} in the
#. translations: the accusative (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty
#. if it is the same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "{count|a wheel of cheese|{count} wheels of cheese}"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cheese keeps the milk of the summer for the winter."
msgstr "Ost gemmer sommerens mælk til vinteren."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/042_a_cow_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A Cow of Our Own"
msgstr "Vores egen ko"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/042_a_cow_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With the east meadow, we have room for a cow at last! Buy one at the horse farm in Torsgården. A "
"cow is big, but she fits in your boat like a crate, if she stands still."
msgstr ""
"Med østengen har vi endelig plads til en ko! Køb en på hestegården på Torsgården. En ko er stor, "
"men hun kan være i båden som en kasse, hvis hun står stille."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/042_a_cow_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Look at her big brown eyes! She will give us milk every day. Let us call her Rosa."
msgstr "Se hendes store brune øjne! Hun giver os mælk hver dag. Lad os kalde hende Rosa."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/042_a_cow_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cows were the wealth of a farm: a family counted its riches in cows."
msgstr "Køer var en gårds rigdom: en familie talte sin rigdom i køer."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/043_pots_for_ekvik/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Pots for Ekvik"
msgstr "Krukker til Ekvik"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/043_pots_for_ekvik/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The fish soup! We cook it for the whole village, but our big pot cracked. Bring us three crates of"
" pots from the potter, please."
msgstr ""
"Fiskesuppen! Vi koger den til hele landsbyen, men vores store gryde revnede. Bring os tre kasser "
"krukker fra pottemageren, tak."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/043_pots_for_ekvik/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "New pots! Tonight there is fish soup for everybody, and for you two the first bowl."
msgstr ""
"Nye krukker! I aften er der fiskesuppe til alle, og {crew|du får den første skål|du får den første"
" skål|I to får de første skåle}."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/043_pots_for_ekvik/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The cooking pot hung over the fire on a chain, and the soup simmered all day."
msgstr "Gryden hang over ilden i en kæde, og suppen simrede hele dagen."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ragna's Broken Oar"
msgstr "Ragnas brækkede åre"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Ragna rowed out at dawn and is not back! I fear her oar broke. Find her on the lakes, then come "
"back and fetch the spare oar for her."
msgstr ""
"Ragna roede ud ved daggry og er ikke kommet tilbage! Jeg er bange for, at hendes åre er brækket. "
"Find hende på søerne, og kom så tilbage og hent reserveåren til hende."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hello! Yes, my oar broke, and I drift with one. Tell Tor to give you the spare one!"
msgstr ""
"Hej! Ja, min åre brækkede, og jeg driver rundt med én. Sig til Tor, at han skal give "
"{crew|dig|dig|jer} reserveåren!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "She is well? Thank the gods. Here is the oar: bring it to her!"
msgstr "Har hun det godt? Gudskelov. Her er åren: bring den til hende!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "My oar! Now I can row again. Here, take some fish: the freshest on the lakes."
msgstr "Min åre! Nu kan jeg ro igen. Her, tag noget fisk: den friskeste på søerne."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Every viking boat carried spare oars: a broken oar was common."
msgstr "Alle vikingebåde havde reserveårer med: en brækket åre skete tit."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Torches for the Dark"
msgstr "Fakler til mørket"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The nights grow long. The guests of the autumn feast need light: bring me tar for torches, two "
"pots from Ekvik, and two crates of flax for the wicks."
msgstr ""
"Nætterne bliver lange. Gæsterne til høstfesten skal have lys: bring mig tjære til fakler, to "
"krukker fra Ekvik, og to kasser hør til vægerne."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Tar for torches? They burn bright and long."
msgstr "Tjære til fakler? De brænder klart og længe."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Tar and flax: now my torches will light up the whole bay!"
msgstr "Tjære og hør: nu lyser mine fakler hele bugten op!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Viking torches were sticks wrapped in flax or cloth, soaked in tar or fat."
msgstr "Vikingernes fakler var pinde viklet ind i hør eller klæde og dyppet i tjære eller fedt."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Autumn Feast"
msgstr "Høstfesten"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The autumn feast is tomorrow! Knut's ale is ready, five barrels. Bring them from Lindtorp, and "
"bring three crates of fish for the soup too."
msgstr ""
"Høstfesten er i morgen! Knuts øl er klar, fem tønder. Hent dem i Lindtorp, og bring også tre "
"kasser fisk til suppen."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The ale! Now the fish."
msgstr "Øllet! Nu fisken."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The biggest batch I ever brewed! Five barrels for Orm."
msgstr "Det største bryg, jeg nogensinde har brygget! Fem tønder til Orm."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ale, soup, torches, Sten's flute and Hrafn's knives! Everybody is here. Dance with us!"
msgstr "Øl, suppe, fakler, Stens fløjte og Hrafns knive! Alle er her. Dans med os!"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json data/missions/077_ale_for_two_inns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "{count|a barrel of ale|{count} barrels of ale}"
msgstr "{count|en tønde øl|{count} tønder øl}"

#. the thing '{count|a barrel of ale|{count} barrels of ale}' for {thing@acc} in the translations:
#. the accusative (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the
#. same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json data/missions/077_ale_for_two_inns/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "{count|a barrel of ale|{count} barrels of ale}"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The autumn feast thanked the gods for the harvest, before the long winter."
msgstr "Høstfesten takkede guderne for høsten før den lange vinter."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/047_the_tipsy_uncle/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Tipsy Uncle"
msgstr "Den lystige onkel"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/047_the_tipsy_uncle/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Uncle Sven of Frosttorp sang and danced all night, and now he can't find his way home! He is very "
"merry and a little wobbly. Row him home to Arne, please."
msgstr ""
"Onkel Sven fra Frosttorp sang og dansede hele natten, og nu kan han ikke finde hjem! Han er meget "
"glad og en lille smule vaklende. Ro ham hjem til Arne, tak."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/047_the_tipsy_uncle/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Uncle Sven! Singing all the way, I hear? Come in, sleep it off. Thank you, girls!"
msgstr ""
"Onkel Sven! Sang hele vejen, hører jeg? Kom ind, og få dig en lur. Tak, {crew|min dreng|min "
"pige|børn|piger}!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/047_the_tipsy_uncle/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Uncle Sven: Ho ho! Two little vikings with a boat! Let us sing on the way!"
msgstr ""
"Onkel Sven: Ho ho! {crew|En lille viking|En lille viking|To små vikinger} med en båd! Lad os synge"
" på vejen!"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/047_the_tipsy_uncle/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Sven"
msgstr "Sven"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/047_the_tipsy_uncle/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Uncle Sven"
msgstr "onkel Sven"

#. the thing 'Uncle Sven' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative (the direct object),
#. e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/047_the_tipsy_uncle/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "Uncle Sven"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/047_the_tipsy_uncle/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The vikings loved songs and riddles; at a feast, everybody had to sing."
msgstr "Vikingerne elskede sange og gåder; til en fest skulle alle synge."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/048_geese_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Geese for the Market"
msgstr "Gæs til markedet"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/048_geese_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The geese of Frosttorp are the fattest on the lakes. I want six for the market! Each goose takes a"
" crate, and they honk all the way."
msgstr ""
"Gæssene fra Frosttorp er de fedeste på søerne. Jeg vil have seks til markedet! Hver gås fylder en "
"kasse, og de snadrer hele vejen."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/048_geese_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Six geese, and not one escaped! The market will be loud today."
msgstr "Seks gæs, og ikke én slap væk! Der bliver larm på markedet i dag."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/048_geese_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Honk! Honk! Hold on to your hats, girls."
msgstr "Gak! Gak! Hold godt fast i huerne, {crew|min dreng|min pige|børn|piger}."

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/048_geese_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Goose"
msgstr "Gås"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/048_geese_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "{count|a goose|{count} geese}"
msgstr "{count|en gås|{count} gæs}"

#. the thing '{count|a goose|{count} geese}' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative
#. (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the
#. plain translation
#: data/missions/048_geese_for_the_market/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "{count|a goose|{count} geese}"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/048_geese_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Geese were kept on viking farms for eggs, feathers and down for pillows."
msgstr "Gæs blev holdt på vikingegårdene for æg, fjer og dun til puder."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/049_the_runestone/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Runestone"
msgstr "Runestenen"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/049_the_runestone/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"I will raise a runestone for my mother. The stone comes from the quarry by Bergö, and the "
"runecarver needs iron chisels from the smith. The stone is so big, it takes three crates of room!"
msgstr ""
"Jeg vil rejse en runesten for min mor. Stenen kommer fra stenbruddet ved Bergö, og runeristeren "
"skal bruge mejsler af jern fra smeden. Stenen er så stor, at den fylder tre kasser!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/049_the_runestone/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Good chisels. Now the stone."
msgstr "Gode mejsler. Nu stenen."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/049_the_runestone/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The stone! The carver begins today."
msgstr "Stenen! Runeristeren begynder i dag."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/049_the_runestone/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "It is in three pieces, to fit in your boat. The carver joins them."
msgstr ""
"Den er i tre stykker, så den kan være i {crew|din|din|jeres} båd. Runeristeren sætter dem sammen."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/049_the_runestone/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The runestone stands! It says: Eirik raised this stone for Gunnvor, his good mother. And at the "
"bottom, small: Ylva and Sigrid rowed it."
msgstr ""
"Runestenen står! Der står: Eirik rejste denne sten for Gunnvor, sin gode mor. Og nederst, med små "
"runer: Ylva og Sigrid roede den."

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/049_the_runestone/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Stone"
msgstr "Sten"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/049_the_runestone/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "{count|a piece of the stone|{count} pieces of the stone}"
msgstr "{count|et stykke af stenen|{count} stykker af stenen}"

#. the thing '{count|a piece of the stone|{count} pieces of the stone}' for {thing@acc} in the
#. translations: the accusative (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty
#. if it is the same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/049_the_runestone/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "{count|a piece of the stone|{count} pieces of the stone}"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/049_the_runestone/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Runestones were raised for loved ones, and painted in bright colours."
msgstr "Runesten blev rejst for kære, og de blev malet i klare farver."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/050_the_first_snow/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The First Snow"
msgstr "Den første sne"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/050_the_first_snow/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Snowflakes! Winter is near. Our store needs feed for the animals: six crates of hay and four of "
"grain. Your hold takes eight: think how to row it!"
msgstr ""
"Snefnug! Vinteren er nær. Vores lager skal have foder til dyrene: seks kasser hø og fire kasser "
"korn. {crew|Dit|Dit|Jeres} lastrum kan tage otte: tænk over, hvordan {crew|du|du|I} ror det hjem!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/050_the_first_snow/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hay for the sheep, the goats and Rosa. Now the grain."
msgstr "Hø til fårene, gederne og Rosa. Nu kornet."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/050_the_first_snow/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The store is full! Let the snow come. Come in, the soup is hot."
msgstr "Lageret er fuldt! Lad bare sneen komme. Kom ind, suppen er varm."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/050_the_first_snow/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "In winter, the animals stayed in the barn for months and ate the hay of the summer."
msgstr "Om vinteren stod dyrene i stalden i månedsvis og spiste sommerens hø."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Ice Breaks"
msgstr "Isen bryder op"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Hear that crack? The ice breaks: spring is here again! Row out and hail two boats: ask how "
"everybody got through the winter."
msgstr ""
"Hører {crew|du|du|I} det knage? Isen bryder op: foråret er her igen! Ro ud, og hils på to både: "
"spørg, hvordan alle er kommet gennem vinteren."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Everybody is well! But Tova has asked for you all winter. Row to Laxön!"
msgstr ""
"Alle har det godt! Men Tova har spurgt efter {crew|dig|dig|jer} hele vinteren. Ro til Laxön!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A long winter! But the herring kept, thanks to your salt."
msgstr "En lang vinter! Men sildene holdt sig, takket være {crew|dit|dit|jeres} salt."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"There you are! Spring is when the animals need us most. Will you be my apprentices, and learn to "
"heal?"
msgstr ""
"Der er {crew|du|du|I}! Om foråret har dyrene mest brug for os. Vil {crew|du være min lærling|du "
"være min lærling|I være mine lærlinge} og lære at helbrede?"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/051_the_ice_breaks/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "When the ice broke in spring, the boats came out, and with them the news."
msgstr "Når isen brød op om foråret, kom bådene ud, og med dem kom nyhederne."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Coughing Horse"
msgstr "Den hostende hest"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Your first case as healers: Ragnfrid's old horse Bror coughs. Take him this syrup of thyme and "
"honey, then come back to me after a night, to hear how he is."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Din|Din|Jeres} første opgave som {crew|helbreder|helbreder|helbredere}: Ragnfrids gamle hest"
" Bror hoster. Bring ham den her sirup af timian og honning, og kom så tilbage til mig efter en nat"
" for at høre, hvordan han har det."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Thyme and honey? Bror loves it. He licks the spoon!"
msgstr "Timian og honning? Det elsker Bror. Han slikker skeen!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "He slept the whole night and coughs no more. Tell Tova: her apprentices are good!"
msgstr "Han sov hele natten og hoster ikke mere. Sig til Tova: hendes lærlinge er dygtige!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
