"{crew|Du er klar|Du er klar|I er klar}. Tag min runde alene i dag: se til lammene i Ålberga, "
"hestene på Torsgården og svanerne i Svanetorp. Kom så og fortæl mig det."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/081_the_healers_round/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "You look in their eyes, their ears, their hooves... All well? Good! They like you."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Du|Du|I} kigger dem i øjnene, ørerne, hovene... Alt vel? Godt! De kan lide "
"{crew|dig|dig|jer}."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/081_the_healers_round/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bror is old, but well. Silke's new foal is strong. Tell Tova all is fine."
msgstr "Bror er gammel, men rask. Silkes nye føl er stærkt. Sig til Tova, at alt er fint."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/081_the_healers_round/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The swans? Fat and happy. One has a sore wing: you wrapped it well."
msgstr "Svanerne? Fede og glade. En har en øm vinge: {crew|du|du|I} har bundet den godt."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/081_the_healers_round/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"All well, and the swan's wing wrapped? Then take this: your own healer's bag. You are healers now."
msgstr ""
"Alt vel, og svanens vinge er bundet? Så tag den her: {crew|din|din|jeres} egen helbrederpose. "
"{crew|Du er helbreder|Du er helbreder|I er helbredere} nu."

#. a gift for a task: 'You get ...'
#: data/missions/081_the_healers_round/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "your own healer's bag"
msgstr "{crew|din|din|jeres} egen helbrederpose"

#. the thing 'your own healer's bag' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative (the direct
#. object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the plain
#. translation
#: data/missions/081_the_healers_round/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "your own healer's bag"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/081_the_healers_round/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Healers looked, listened and touched: they had no tools but their hands and their herbs."
msgstr "Helbrederne kiggede, lyttede og følte: de havde intet værktøj ud over hænderne og urterne."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/082_the_colt_in_the_mud/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Colt in the Mud"
msgstr "Hingsteføllet i mudderet"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/082_the_colt_in_the_mud/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Silke's colt ran into the bog and is stuck to his belly! I need a long rope: Tor in Stormvik has "
"the longest. Hurry, he is scared!"
msgstr ""
"Silkes hingsteføl løb ud i mosen og sidder fast til maven! Jeg skal bruge et langt reb: Tor i "
"Stormvik har det længste. Skynd {crew|dig|dig|jer}, han er bange!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/082_the_colt_in_the_mud/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Rope around him, gently, everybody pull... Slurp! He is out! Muddy, but well. You saved him."
msgstr ""
"Reb om ham, forsigtigt, alle trækker... Slurp! Han er ude! Mudret, men rask. {crew|Du|Du|I} "
"reddede ham."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/082_the_colt_in_the_mud/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "My longest rope! Take it, quick!"
msgstr "Mit længste reb! Tag det, hurtigt!"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/082_the_colt_in_the_mud/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Rope"
msgstr "Reb"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/082_the_colt_in_the_mud/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "the long rope"
msgstr "det lange reb"

#. the thing 'the long rope' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative (the direct
#. object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the plain
#. translation
#: data/missions/082_the_colt_in_the_mud/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "the long rope"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/082_the_colt_in_the_mud/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A horse stuck in mud must be pulled out slowly, or it hurts its legs."
msgstr ""
"En hest, der sidder fast i mudder, skal trækkes langsomt op, ellers gør den skade på benene."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/083_grain_for_the_north/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Grain for the North"
msgstr "Korn til Norden"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/083_grain_for_the_north/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My hunters send news: the summer in the north was cold, and their families have no grain. My ship "
"leaves in three days: fill it with twelve crates!"
msgstr ""
"Mine jægere sender bud: sommeren i nord var kold, og deres familier har intet korn. Mit skib "
"sejler om tre dage: fyld det med tolv kasser!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/083_grain_for_the_north/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Twelve crates! Nobody in the north goes hungry this winter. The whole valley thanks you."
msgstr "Tolv kasser! Ingen i nord sulter i vinter. Hele dalen takker {crew|dig|dig|jer}."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/083_grain_for_the_north/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "When the harvest failed, the farms helped each other: next year, it might be them."
msgstr "Når høsten slog fejl, hjalp gårdene hinanden: næste år kunne det være dem selv."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/084_the_wool_fair/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Wool Fair"
msgstr "Uldmarkedet"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/084_the_wool_fair/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The wool fair! Traders come from the Long Lake to buy. Bring me eight crates of wool, the more the"
" better, and the fair is a success."
msgstr ""
"Uldmarkedet! Handelsfolk kommer fra Langsøen for at købe. Bring mig otte kasser uld, jo flere jo "
"bedre, så bliver markedet en succes."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/084_the_wool_fair/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Eight crates! The traders from the Long Lake ask: who are these girls? I say: the best traders of "
"the Home Lakes."
msgstr ""
"Otte kasser! Handelsfolkene fra Langsøen spørger: hvem er {crew|den dreng|den pige|de børn|de "
"piger}? Jeg siger: {crew|den bedste handelsmand|den bedste handelskvinde|de bedste handelsfolk|de "
"bedste handelskvinder} på Hjemsøerne."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/084_the_wool_fair/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Wool was so important that some sagas tell of whole ships full of it."
msgstr "Uld var så vigtigt, at nogle sagaer fortæller om hele skibe fulde af det."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Goats on the Island"
msgstr "Gederne på øen"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My four goats swam to Bergö! They eat Dagny's flowers, and she is cross. Bring them back before "
"they eat her kiln too!"
msgstr ""
"Mine fire geder svømmede til Bergö! De spiser Dagnys blomster, og hun er vred. Hent dem tilbage, "
"før de også spiser hendes ovn!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "My naughty goats! Tomorrow I build a higher fence. Here, my best cheese."
msgstr "Mine uartige geder! I morgen bygger jeg et højere hegn. Her, min bedste ost."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Take them, take them! They ate my flowers and a basket and a shoe!"
msgstr "Tag dem, tag dem! De spiste mine blomster og en kurv og en sko!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Goats are good swimmers when they must be, and they eat nearly anything."
msgstr "Geder er gode svømmere, når de skal, og de spiser næsten alt."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "News for Everybody"
msgstr "Nyt til alle"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Big news: a ship from the Long Lake will come, and the way between the lakes opens! Tell the "
"smith, the fishers of Stormvik and Orm in Hallvik. I tell the rest."
msgstr ""
"Store nyheder: et skib fra Langsøen kommer, og vejen mellem søerne åbner! Sig det til smeden, "
"fiskerne i Stormvik og Orm i Hallvik. Jeg siger det til resten."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A ship from the Long Lake? They will want my iron!"
msgstr "Et skib fra Langsøen? De vil have mit jern!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "New lakes, new fish! Thank you for telling us."
msgstr "Nye søer, nye fisk! Tak, fordi {crew|du|du|I} fortalte os det."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Guests from far away! I must brew more. Thank you, girls!"
msgstr "Gæster langvejs fra! Jeg må brygge mere. Tak, {crew|min dreng|min pige|børn|piger}!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The lakes of the north were joined by rivers and portages, where boats were dragged over land."
msgstr "Søerne i Norden var forbundet af floder og bæresteder, hvor bådene blev slæbt over land."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A Cow for Grim"
msgstr "En ko til Grim"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"I am old, and I would like fresh milk every morning. Bring me a cow from the horse farm. The swans"
" will be jealous!"
msgstr ""
"Jeg er gammel, og jeg vil gerne have frisk mælk hver morgen. Bring mig en ko fra hestegården. "
"Svanerne bliver misundelige!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A cow! I call her Swan, ha. Here, for your trouble, and for all the years you visited an old man."
msgstr ""
"En ko! Jeg kalder hende Svane, ha. Her, for {crew|din|din|jeres} ulejlighed, og for alle de år, "
"{crew|du|du|I} har besøgt en gammel mand."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A good cow gave milk for ten years or more, and was part of the family."
msgstr "En god ko gav mælk i ti år eller mere og hørte til familien."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flowers on the Hill"
msgstr "Blomster på bakken"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Plant flowers on the sunny hill! When they bloom, bring three crates to Gudrun's inn: she wants "
"the inn to smell like summer."
msgstr ""
"Så blomster på den solrige bakke! Når de blomstrer, så bring tre kasser til Gudruns kro: hun vil "
"have, at kroen dufter af sommer."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flower seeds in the earth. In two days, they bloom."
msgstr "Blomsterfrø i jorden. Om to dage blomstrer de."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Flowers on every table! The guests smile. Here is your silver, and a cup of milk for each of you."
msgstr ""
"Blomster på hvert bord! Gæsterne smiler. Her er {crew|dit|dit|jeres} sølv, og {crew|et krus "
"mælk|et krus mælk|et krus mælk til hver}."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Vikings wove flowers into wreaths and crowns for feasts and weddings."
msgstr "Vikingerne bandt blomster til kranse og kroner til fester og bryllupper."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Pottery Market"
msgstr "Marked for krukker"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The new kiln makes so many pots! Bring ten crates to the market in Kråkhamn. Ten crates: only your"
" big boat can do it."
msgstr ""
"Den nye ovn laver så mange krukker! Bring ti kasser til markedet i Kråkhamn. Ti kasser: kun "
"{crew|din|din|jeres} store båd kan klare det."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ten crates of Dagny's pots, and not one broken! The best rowing of the lakes."
msgstr "Ti kasser af Dagnys krukker, og ikke én er gået i stykker! Den bedste roning på søerne."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Pack them in straw: pots do not like to bump!"
msgstr "Pak dem i halm: krukker kan ikke lide at blive stødt!"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Pots"
msgstr "Krukker"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "{count|a crate of pots|{count} crates of pots}"
msgstr "{count|en kasse krukker|{count} kasser krukker}"

#. the thing '{count|a crate of pots|{count} crates of pots}' for {thing@acc} in the translations:
#. the accusative (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the
#. same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "{count|a crate of pots|{count} crates of pots}"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Clay pots were carried packed in straw, so that they did not break."
msgstr "Lerkrukker blev fragtet pakket i halm, så de ikke gik i stykker."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Gudrun's Ring"
msgstr "Gudruns ring"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My mother's ring! It slipped from my finger into the lake, by the jetty. Gone forever... unless a "
"fisher's net caught it? Ask Ragna."
msgstr ""
"Min mors ring! Den gled af min finger og ned i søen ved bryggen. Væk for altid... medmindre et "
"fiskernet har fanget den? Spørg Ragna."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A ring? Wait... Tor found something shiny in our net yesterday! Ask him in Stormvik."
msgstr "En ring? Vent... Tor fandt noget skinnende i vores net i går! Spørg ham i Stormvik."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My mother's ring! Back from the lake! I can not thank you enough. Every meal at my inn is free for"
" you."
msgstr ""
"Min mors ring! Tilbage fra søen! Jeg kan ikke takke {crew|dig|dig|jer} nok. Hvert måltid på min "
"kro er gratis for {crew|dig|dig|jer}."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "This? Silver with a little red stone. I thought it was a fish's treasure!"
msgstr "Den her? Sølv med en lille rød sten. Jeg troede, det var en fisks skat!"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ring"
msgstr "Ring"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "the ring"
msgstr "ringen"

#. the thing 'the ring' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative (the direct object),
#. e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "the ring"
msgstr ""

#. a gift for a task: 'You get ...'
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "free meals at the inn of Vargvik"
msgstr "gratis mad på kroen i Vargvik"

#. the thing 'free meals at the inn of Vargvik' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative
#. (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the
#. plain translation
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "free meals at the inn of Vargvik"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Vikings sometimes gave silver to the lakes on purpose, as gifts to the gods."
msgstr "Vikingerne gav nogle gange sølv til søerne med vilje, som gaver til guderne."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Edge of the Forest"
msgstr "Skovbrynet"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Kol and Ingrid want sheep for their new home. Bring them two sheep, and I give you the strip of "
"land by the forest, next to your farm. A fair trade!"
msgstr ""
"Kol og Ingrid vil have får til deres nye hjem. Bring dem to får, så giver jeg {crew|dig|dig|jer} "
"jordstykket ved skoven, lige ved siden af {crew|din|din|jeres} gård. En fair handel!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Two sheep for the young ones! Ingrid already knits. The forest edge is yours: good wood and two "
"fields."
msgstr ""
"To får til de unge! Ingrid strikker allerede. Skovbrynet er {crew|dit|dit|jeres}: godt træ og to "
"marker."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Land was traded for animals, silver or work: there were no banks."
msgstr "Jord blev byttet for dyr, sølv eller arbejde: der var ingen banker."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Longhouse Grows"
msgstr "Langhuset vokser"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With so many animals and friends, our house is too small! Bring twelve logs from Frosttorp, two "
"crates of tools and two pots of tar, and we make it longer."
msgstr ""
"Med så mange dyr og venner er vores hus for lille! Bring tolv stammer fra Frosttorp, to kasser "
"værktøj og to krukker tjære, så gør vi det længere."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Twelve logs! Fill that big hold of yours."
msgstr "Tolv stammer! Fyld {crew|dit|dit|jeres} store lastrum."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Axes and nails. Now the tar for the roof."
msgstr "Økser og søm. Nu tjæren til taget."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hammering all night with the neighbours... Our longhouse is twice as long! Room for a feast."
msgstr "Hamren hele natten med naboerne... Vores langhus er dobbelt så langt! Plads til en fest."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A longhouse could be made longer by adding a piece at the end, like a train."
msgstr "Et langhus kunne gøres længere ved at bygge et stykke til for enden, ligesom et tog."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Green Valley"
msgstr "Den grønne dal"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You helped my valley all year. The green valley behind your farm has no owner: bring me two crates"
" of cloth and two of honey for the gods' feast, and it is yours."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Du|Du|I} har hjulpet min dal hele året. Den grønne dal bag {crew|din|din|jeres} gård har "
"ingen ejer: bring mig to kasser klæde og to kasser honning til gudernes fest, så er den "
"{crew|din|din|jeres}."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cloth for the hall. Now the honey."
msgstr "Klæde til hallen. Nu honningen."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Father says it at the Thing, in front of everybody: the green valley belongs to Ylva and Sigrid!"
msgstr "Far siger det på tinget, foran alle: den grønne dal tilhører Ylva og Sigrid!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "At the Thing, the meeting of the free people, land and laws were decided."
msgstr "På tinget, de frie folks møde, blev der besluttet om jord og love."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bees for the Valley"
msgstr "Bier til dalen"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The valley is full of clover and heather. Bees would love it! Have three beehives on the farm, and"
" we will have honey all year."
msgstr ""
"Dalen er fuld af kløver og lyng. Bierne ville elske den! Hav tre bistader på gården, så har vi "
